<title>USA: Marion Cty, Fla., tax vote postponed to Sept. 2.</title>
<headline>Marion Cty, Fla., tax vote postponed to Sept. 2.</headline>
<dateline>OCALA, Fla. 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Florida's Marion County has postponed until Sept. 2 a referendum on a half-cent sales tax for schools, elections supervisors said.</p>
<p>The special election originally was set for June 10. The tax would raise an estimated $58 million over five years to fund construction of five new schools, renovation at 16 schools and add $20 million worth of technological equipment.</p>
<p>((--Jane Sutton, 305-374-5013))</p>
